WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.810
- [Narrator] Juul Labs was once

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.560
one of the most valuable
startups in the world,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.503
valued in 2018 at $38 billion.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.200
But most of that has gone up in smoke.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.840
In 2020, Altria, which holds
a 35% stake in the company

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.408
said Juul is now worth
less than $5 billion.

00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:20.590
- Juul's been a fascinating story to cover

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:24.060
because it rose and fell so quickly.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.060
It really turned the tobacco
industry upside down overnight.

00:00:29.335 --> 00:00:31.210
- [Narrator] Juul is
fighting for its life,

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.000
laying off in the past year
around 3/4 of its employees.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.840
It faces hundreds of lawsuits

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.370
alleging the company marketed
its products to teens.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.100
- If you think you can
come into this county

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.500
and you can harm our youth

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.020
and we're not gonna fight
you back, you're wrong.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.050
- [Narrator] It's product's
popularity with young people

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.560
has become the liability

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.783
that's a threat to the
company's viability.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:59.060
In 2015, Juul introduced a new vaporizer.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.130
The company was founded

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.340
by Stanford University graduate students

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.170
Adam Bowen, and James Monsees.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.270
- Adam and I smoked.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.400
We tried to quit and we failed.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.870
For us, giving up smoking

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:14.510
required an alternative which
did not exist at the time.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:16.870
We founded Juul Labs to invent one.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.290
- Adam Bowen and James
Monsees developed a product

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.150
that was unlike any e-cigarette
that came before it.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.360
It had a cool, sleek, slim design

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.600
that looked like a USB flash drive,

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.710
and they were going for an
aesthetic like an Apple product.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.070
They wanted to have something
that was high tech, cool,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.210
that people would wanna be seen holding.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:41.010
The secret sauce was
also what was inside it.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.800
It contained a nicotine salt solution

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.830
that delivered a really
powerful punch of nicotine,

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.410
but without the throat harshness

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.140
that you might otherwise expect

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.740
from an e-cigarette at the time.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:55.420
- [Narrator] In 2016,
legacy tobacco firms,

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.310
with their similar looking products,

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:59.720
led the pack in e-cigarette sales.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.730
That year, Juul sold 2.2 million devices.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.370
It was still a small player.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.780
But in 2017, that changed.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.230
Juul's sales numbers soared that year,

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:11.320
increasing nearly eight fold.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.840
- It was available in
more and more stores,

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.600
many convenience stores and gas stations.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.420
So that helped propel its growth
and Juul also marketed it.

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:23.840
They gave Juul packages to celebrities

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.540
for as little as a dollar

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.020
to try to get them to use
it and be seen using it

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:30.380
in the hopes that celebrities

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.010
and other social media influencers

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.290
would help spread the word.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.620
- [Narrator] As Juul's own
data would later disclose,

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.040
some of the customers its
product was attracting

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.510
had never smoked cigarettes before.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.920
By the end of 2018, Juul Labs had captured

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.920
68% of the $1.9 billion
US e-cigarette market.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.420
Prominent investors took notice.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.800
A fundraising round that summer

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.100
brought the startup's
value to about $16 billion.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.970
But 2018 was also the
year Juul found itself

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.380
in the crosshairs of regulators.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.810
The Food and Drug Administration

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.690
opened an investigation into Juul

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.750
after parents and school administrators

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.580
sounded the alarm about youth vaping.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:13.120
After two decades of declining
teen cigarette smoking,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.320
a 2018 survey revealed that
the share of high schoolers

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.160
who were vaping had
increased significantly.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:24.160
- When the regulator in charge
of the e-cigarette industry

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.810
targets your company, that's a big deal.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.980
And Juul took a series of steps that year

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:37.200
to try to show that they were
taking the problem seriously.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.140
The first thing they did

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.930
was they said that they
would work with retailers

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:44.460
to ensure that at the point of sale

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.020
kids weren't getting access to
Juul and other e-cigarettes.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.000
- [Narrator] But the FDA wasn't satisfied.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.930
It conducted an inspection
at the company's headquarters

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:55.640
and the agency threatened to
take flavored e-cigarettes

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:57.080
off the market entirely

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.130
because they were
attracting underage users.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:04.850
- Juul responded by voluntarily pulling

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.250
most of their sweet and fruity flavors

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.740
out of brick and mortar retail stores.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.230
So those flavors included Mango Cucumber

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.400
and Creme Brulee, for example.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:20.400
Juul also suspended its social
media marketing in the US.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.480
- [Narrator] Despite all this,

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.360
Juul's valuation soared to $38 billion

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.560
when Altria, the maker of Marlboro,

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:30.370
bought a significant minority
stake in the company.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.000
- Altria wanted to get a piece

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.280
of the growing e-cigarette market

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.470
and Altria's own e-cigarette products

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.120
were not that successful.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.960
- [Narrator] Altria got in
at an inauspicious moment.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.530
After making the nearly $13
billion investment in Juul,

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:46.080
things began to unwind.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.600
Rite Aid, the third
largest us pharmacy chain,

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.050
announced it would stop selling
e-cigarettes in its stores.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:56.620
In September 2019, Juul CEO
Kevin Burns stepped down.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:00.580
He was replaced by Altria
executive K.C. Crosthwaite.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:01.413
That same month,

00:05:01.413 --> 00:05:03.940
in a blow to the company's
overseas ambitions,

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:06.450
China, the world's biggest tobacco market,

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.610
halted Juul's sales just
days after its launch there.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.550
And in the US, governors
called for immediate bans

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.770
on all flavored e-cigarettes.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:19.500
- Common sense says if you
don't know what you are smoking,

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.940
don't smoke it.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:21.773
- [Narrator] At the same time,

00:05:21.773 --> 00:05:23.810
the entire nicotine vaping industry

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:26.370
faced a full blown PR crisis.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:27.870
- New vaping numbers.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.810
Illnesses top 1,000
with deaths on the rise.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:33.730
- Some patients actually
suffered toxic chemical burns

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:34.810
to their lungs and airways,

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.000
as if being exposed to a chemical spill.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.550
- [Narrator] After hospitals
throughout the country

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.840
linked at least eight deaths to vaping,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.710
US health officials urged Americans

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:45.900
to stop using any and
all e-cigarette products

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.100
while authorities investigated the cause.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.540
The illnesses were eventually linked

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:53.130
to marijuana vaping devices
containing vitamin E oil,

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.940
not to e-cigarettes like Juul,

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:58.200
but the damage to vaping's
image continued to be felt

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.560
and the tsunami of bad
news for Juul continued.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.690
Juul's new CEO halted most US advertising,

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:06.440
then stopped all US sales

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.830
of Juul's sweet and fruity flavors.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:10.810
State attorneys general across the country

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:14.620
sued Juul for deceptive
marketing of its products.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.040
- Juul basically took a page
from big tobacco's playbook

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:19.700
by marketing its products

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.040
in a manner that was
appealing to underage youth.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.730
- [Narrator] In court
filings, experts alleged

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.700
that even though the models Juul used

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:29.600
in its 2015 promotional
materials were in their 20s,

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:31.910
they appeared in poses and behaviors

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.860
more characteristic of underage
teens than mature adults.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:38.130
Crosthwaite was grilled by lawmakers

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.710
for the marketing methods Juul
employed before he arrived.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:45.570
- We are focused on
combating underage access.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.420
'Cause it know it puts it all at risk

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.420
if we don't make progress here.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.090
- Sir, how do I trust
what you say? (scoffs)

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.303
- My actions, so far since I've joined,

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:58.560
support our recognition
that more needed to be done.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.850
- [Narrator] More done with fewer people.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.403
Amid a sharp drop in
sales in the fall of 2020,

00:07:03.403 --> 00:07:06.080
Juul continued to shrink its workforce

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:10.450
down to around 1,000 from
its high of just over 4,000

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:13.180
and pulled out of most overseas markets.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:15.840
And Altria wrote down the
value of its stake in Juul

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.260
by around $11 billion.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:22.070
- Everything hinges on an FDA review

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:24.860
that will determine whether
or not Juul's products

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:28.890
can stay on the market or
whether they have to come off.

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:33.890
It presented a real potential
for a public health benefit.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:37.120
You know, getting adult cigarette smokers

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:42.120
off of cigarettes, which
kill 480,000 people a year,

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.520
you know, offered a lot of promise.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.290
It was interesting to investors,

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:50.090
it was compelling to
public health experts,

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:53.940
but at the same time, Juul
presented an incredible risk.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.120
- [Narrator] Federal data now show

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.380
that youth vaping is decreasing.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:01.120
The CEO said Juul is now focused
on its founding principle,

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.970
to help smokers move away from cigarettes.

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.930
But that Juul needs to
prove it can be trusted.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:09.000
If it can do that, Crosthwaite said,

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.950
Juul has a lot of
potential in the longterm.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.850
But that will be an uphill battle.

00:08:13.850 --> 00:08:16.485
(intense music)

